<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Lint stays enabled and fatal: a lint error fails CI exactly as a compile error
  does. Two checks are silenced, each for a stated reason — not to make the build
  green.

  GradleDependency: "a newer version exists" is not a defect. The AndroidX
  versions are pinned to a combination verified to build together; bumping them
  one at a time because lint suggested it is how a Compose project acquires an
  unresolvable dependency graph.

  OldTargetApi: target SDK 35 is chosen for a POCO X3 Pro on Android 13. Chasing
  each new platform release would silently change runtime behaviour on the
  device this app exists for.

  Everything else — Compose correctness, accessibility, scoped storage — is
  reported and still fails the build.
-->
<lint>
    <issue id="GradleDependency" severity="ignore" />
    <issue id="OldTargetApi" severity="ignore" />
</lint>
